This MOD adds more infantry and artillery unit types to Hearts of Iron IV, enriching the diversity of land warfare units.
[list]
[*][b]Light Infantry[/b] - High mobility reconnaissance infantry units, good at fighting in complex terrain.
[*][b]Garrison Troops[/b] - Low-cost defensive infantry, especially suitable for garrison missions, with severe terrain attack and movement penalties, completely unable to be used for offensive operations.
[*][b]Militia Battalion[/b] - Low-cost rapid training units, with very low attack but some defensive capability suitable for early defensive operations.
[*][b]Heavy Infantry Battalion[/b] - Heavy infantry units equipped with artillery, with stronger firepower, equivalent to infantry with half an artillery support company built-in.
[*][b]Combined Arms Battalion[/b] - Early combined arms units with multiple military branches, powerful firepower but disorganized structure
[*][b]Motorized Combined Arms Battalion[/b] - Highly mobile combined units, vehicle transport support weapons
[*][b]Mechanized Combined Arms Battalion[/b] - Advanced combined arms infantry units using armored personnel carriers
[*][b]Airborne Artillery Brigade[/b] - Air-droppable light artillery units, providing long-range fire support
[*][b]Airborne Anti-Tank Brigade[/b] - Air-droppable anti-tank units, specifically designed to counter enemy armor forces
[*][b]Fortress Engineers[/b] - Completely sacrificing offensive capability in exchange for extremely high entrenchment value (100), can work with low-cost units to construct long-term fixed defensive lines.
[/list]

[h3]Combined Arms Unit Explanation[/h3]
This mod contains a series of [b]Combined Arms Battalions[/b] with extremely strong offensive capabilities. These units integrate various supporting firepower, but due to their great command difficulty, they will have very harsh [b]penalties[/b] in the early stages of the game, including larger [b]combat width[/b], higher [b]supply consumption[/b], and lower [b]organization[/b], etc., to reflect the difficulties of initial unit coordination. Players need to research specialized [b]Combined Arms Doctrines[/b] to gradually reduce these penalties and ultimately unlock the true combat potential of these units.

[h3]Mod Declaration[/h3]
[b]1. Compatibility: No original game files have been modified, theoretically compatible with all mods, but balance values are only adjusted for the vanilla game.[/b]
[b]2. Secondary Development:[/b] Anyone is allowed to freely use, modify or develop this mod further.
[b]3. Feedback Suggestions:[/b] Bug feedback in the discussion section is welcome, or share your creative ideas about new units and balance!
[b]4. Localization Notes:[/b] This mod uses AI to generate localization files in multiple commonly used languages, there may be translation flaws, corrections are welcome.

[h3]Q&A[/h3]
[b]Why can't Militia receive doctrine bonuses?[/b]
Because in the official doctrines, militia bonuses are hardcoded into the militia units themselves rather than the category, and for compatibility reasons, original game files are not planned to be modified.

